<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src &#39;none&#39;; style-src &#39;sha256-p5QlDHJVF3Ko1mOmUXIAztSwof3lbSBiwcY0WZXL9tM=&#39;; img-src &#39;none&#39;; font-src &#39;none&#39;; base-uri &#39;none&#39;; form-action &#39;none&#39;">
<meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Accessibility summary for Example Goods</title>
<style>@page { size: A4; margin: 18mm 16mm; }
:root { color-scheme: light; }
html { background: #ffffff; color: #1b1b1b; }
body { font: 11pt/1.5 system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Noto Sans", "Liberation Sans", Arial, sans-serif; font-variant-ligatures: none; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 46rem; padding: 1.5rem; }
h1 { font-size: 1.7rem; line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
h2 { font-size: 1.3rem; margin: 2rem 0 0.5rem; break-after: avoid; }
h3 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 1.25rem 0 0.4rem; break-after: avoid; }
p, ul, ol { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
li { margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
a { color: #0b4f8a; text-decoration: underline; }
.meta { color: #4a4a4a; }
.figures { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
.figures li { border-left: 4px solid #0b4f8a; padding-left: 0.6rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
figure { margin: 1rem 0; break-inside: avoid; }
figcaption { font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
svg.chart { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; max-width: 40rem; }
.chart .axis, .chart .grid { stroke: #767676; stroke-width: 1; }
.chart .grid { stroke-dasharray: 2 3; }
.chart .label { fill: #1b1b1b; font-size: 12px; }
.chart .line { fill: none; stroke: #0b4f8a; stroke-width: 2.5; }
.chart .point { fill: #0b4f8a; }
.chart .bar-critical { fill: #9b1c1c; }
.chart .bar-serious { fill: #a3470d; }
.chart .bar-moderate { fill: #6b5300; }
.chart .bar-minor { fill: #3d4f63; }
table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem; font-size: 0.95em; }
caption { text-align: left; font-weight: 600; padding-bottom: 0.3rem; }
th, td { border: 1px solid #767676; padding: 0.3rem 0.5rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
th[scope="col"] { background: #f2f2f2; }
td.num, th.num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
tr { break-inside: avoid; }</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
<h1>Accessibility summary for Example Goods</h1>
<p class="meta">Results from September 1, 2026 to October 17, 2026. Prepared on October 18, 2026.</p>
<h2>Key figures</h2>
<ul class="figures">
<li>No scan has finished yet, so there are no results to show.</li>
<li>20 open findings</li>
<li>0 fixes verified in this period</li>
<li>1 proposed fix waiting for approval</li>
</ul>
<h2>Automated pass rate over time</h2>
<p>No scan has finished yet, so there are no results to show.</p>
<h2>Open findings by impact</h2>
<figure>
<figcaption id="impact-caption">Open findings from the latest scan, by impact</figcaption>
<svg class="chart" role="img" aria-labelledby="impact-caption impact-summary" viewBox="0 0 640 208" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" focusable="false">
<line class="axis" x1="112" x2="112" y1="8" y2="200"/>
<text class="label" x="104" y="36" text-anchor="end">Critical</text>
<rect class="bar-critical" x="112" y="16" width="51.6" height="32"/>
<text class="label" x="171.6" y="36">1</text>
<text class="label" x="104" y="84" text-anchor="end">Serious</text>
<rect class="bar-serious" x="112" y="64" width="309.3" height="32"/>
<text class="label" x="429.3" y="84">6</text>
<text class="label" x="104" y="132" text-anchor="end">Moderate</text>
<rect class="bar-moderate" x="112" y="112" width="464.0" height="32"/>
<text class="label" x="584.0" y="132">9</text>
<text class="label" x="104" y="180" text-anchor="end">Minor</text>
<rect class="bar-minor" x="112" y="160" width="206.2" height="32"/>
<text class="label" x="326.2" y="180">4</text>
</svg>
<p id="impact-summary">Bar chart of open findings by impact: 1 critical, 6 serious, 9 moderate and 4 minor. The table below has the same numbers.</p>
</figure>
<table>
<caption>Open findings from the latest scan, by impact</caption>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Impact</th><th scope="col" class="num">Open findings</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">Critical</th><td class="num">1</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Serious</th><td class="num">6</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Moderate</th><td class="num">9</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Minor</th><td class="num">4</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Total</th><td class="num">20</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h2>What the automated checks cover</h2>
<p>WCAG 2.2 has 55 success criteria at Level A and AA. Each one below is either tested by automated checks, tested only in part, or not tested by automated checks at all.</p>
<h3>Tested by automated checks: 0 criteria</h3>
<p>None.</p>
<h3>Tested in part; a person must check the rest: 25 criteria</h3>
<ul>
<li>1.1.1 Non-text Content (Level A)</li>
<li>1.2.2 Captions (Prerecorded) (Level A)</li>
<li>1.3.1 Info and Relationships (Level A)</li>
<li>1.3.5 Identify Input Purpose (Level AA)</li>
<li>1.4.1 Use of Color (Level A)</li>
<li>1.4.2 Audio Control (Level A)</li>
<li>1.4.3 Contrast (Minimum) (Level AA)</li>
<li>1.4.4 Resize Text (Level AA)</li>
<li>1.4.10 Reflow (Level AA)</li>
<li>1.4.12 Text Spacing (Level AA)</li>
<li>2.1.1 Keyboard (Level A)</li>
<li>2.1.2 No Keyboard Trap (Level A)</li>
<li>2.2.1 Timing Adjustable (Level A)</li>
<li>2.2.2 Pause, Stop, Hide (Level A)</li>
<li>2.4.1 Bypass Blocks (Level A)</li>
<li>2.4.2 Page Titled (Level A)</li>
<li>2.4.4 Link Purpose (In Context) (Level A)</li>
<li>2.4.7 Focus Visible (Level AA)</li>
<li>2.4.11 Focus Not Obscured (Minimum) (Level AA)</li>
<li>2.5.3 Label in Name (Level A)</li>
<li>2.5.8 Target Size (Minimum) (Level AA)</li>
<li>3.1.1 Language of Page (Level A)</li>
<li>3.1.2 Language of Parts (Level AA)</li>
<li>3.3.2 Labels or Instructions (Level A)</li>
<li>4.1.2 Name, Role, Value (Level A)</li>
</ul>
<h3>Not tested by automated checks; a person must check: 30 criteria</h3>
<ul>
<li>1.2.1 Audio-only and Video-only (Prerecorded) (Level A)</li>
<li>1.2.3 Audio Description or Media Alternative (Prerecorded) (Level A)</li>
<li>1.2.4 Captions (Live) (Level AA)</li>
<li>1.2.5 Audio Description (Prerecorded) (Level AA)</li>
<li>1.3.2 Meaningful Sequence (Level A)</li>
<li>1.3.3 Sensory Characteristics (Level A)</li>
<li>1.3.4 Orientation (Level AA)</li>
<li>1.4.5 Images of Text (Level AA)</li>
<li>1.4.11 Non-text Contrast (Level AA)</li>
<li>1.4.13 Content on Hover or Focus (Level AA)</li>
<li>2.1.4 Character Key Shortcuts (Level A)</li>
<li>2.3.1 Three Flashes or Below Threshold (Level A)</li>
<li>2.4.3 Focus Order (Level A)</li>
<li>2.4.5 Multiple Ways (Level AA)</li>
<li>2.4.6 Headings and Labels (Level AA)</li>
<li>2.5.1 Pointer Gestures (Level A)</li>
<li>2.5.2 Pointer Cancellation (Level A)</li>
<li>2.5.4 Motion Actuation (Level A)</li>
<li>2.5.7 Dragging Movements (Level AA)</li>
<li>3.2.1 On Focus (Level A)</li>
<li>3.2.2 On Input (Level A)</li>
<li>3.2.3 Consistent Navigation (Level AA)</li>
<li>3.2.4 Consistent Identification (Level AA)</li>
<li>3.2.6 Consistent Help (Level A)</li>
<li>3.3.1 Error Identification (Level A)</li>
<li>3.3.3 Error Suggestion (Level AA)</li>
<li>3.3.4 Error Prevention (Legal, Financial, Data) (Level AA)</li>
<li>3.3.7 Redundant Entry (Level A)</li>
<li>3.3.8 Accessible Authentication (Minimum) (Level AA)</li>
<li>4.1.3 Status Messages (Level AA)</li>
</ul>
<p>3 results that the automated checks could not decide are waiting for a person to review. They are counted neither as failures nor as passes.</p>
<p class="meta">Checks used: axe-core 4.14.0 + rampsmith-rules 0f3c9a1.</p>
<h2>About these results</h2>
<p>Automated testing finds only part of all accessibility barriers. Deque, the maker of the axe-core engine these checks use, reports that axe-core finds on average 57% of WCAG issues. The rest need a person to check.</p>
<p>A check is one automated rule for WCAG 2.2 Level A or AA, tested on one page in one state. The pass rate is the checks passed divided by the checks run in that scan. Results waiting for a person to review are not counted.</p>
<p>Impact is the severity the checks assign: critical and serious barriers block tasks for some people; moderate and minor ones make tasks harder.</p>

</main>
</body>
</html>
